WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.402
-I want to get
that truck that --

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.869
You know,
Biden was at that Ford thing.

00:00:03.869 --> 00:00:05.504
-Oh, the electric truck?
-The electric truck.

00:00:05.504 --> 00:00:06.572
I've got to get it.
I want to get it.

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:07.673
And I looked into it.

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:08.774
Because, you know,
I'm a truck driver.

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:10.643
-You're super-trucky.

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.312
-I am. I've got an F-150.
-Yep.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:13.846
-Ask me how big my truck is.

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:15.047
-How big is your truck?

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:17.183
-Big enough.
-Nice.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:19.752
-But I looked into this,
'cause I got my truck

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:23.289
because I wanted to haul
pumpkins around pumpkin season.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.191
-Pumpkin lattes or pumpkins?

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.692
-Pumpkin season --
Pumpkins, man.

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:27.961
Pumpkin season comes, what are
you gonna do?

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:29.295
Put a towel down
in the back seat?

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:32.265
-No. You'd look like a fool.
You got to get a truck.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:35.602
-I strap it into the kids' seat
and make sure the pumpkin --

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:38.003
I don't have room for a pumpkin.
-Ridiculous. Ridiculous.

00:00:38.003 --> 00:00:39.905
-You get a Ford F-150,

00:00:39.905 --> 00:00:41.474
you can throw like
100 pumpkins in the back.

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:42.575
-1,000 pumpkins.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.543
You get a trailer hitch,
you're set.

00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:46.478
-Yeah. Anyways, I love it.

00:00:46.478 --> 00:00:49.415
It's bigger than my first
studio apartment, definitely.

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.918
It is the most roomiest,
best thing in the world.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:52.952
I love it so much.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.587
But, anyways,
this new one is the jam,

00:00:55.587 --> 00:00:57.257
this new electric one.

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:58.524
They're just announcing it.

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:02.262
So, it's the fastest
acceleration of any F-150 --

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:04.764
zero to 60 in 4 1/2 seconds.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:07.033
-Ooh! There goes
the pumpkins out the back.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.834
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:10.170
And then, that's how
you make pumpkin latte.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.237
-Exactly.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.906
-Yeah. Forgot to
put the hatch up, yeah.

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:16.742
Tows up to 10,000 pounds.

00:01:16.742 --> 00:01:18.243
So I don't even have to have
the pumpkins in my truck.

00:01:18.243 --> 00:01:21.347
-No. You have a trailer
and 10,000 pounds a pumpkin,

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:25.217
guess what --
you're set for a week.

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:26.652
-No, this is the thing
that I wanted to talk about

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:27.921
that I looked into.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:30.422
Listen to this. It's electric.
-Yep.

00:01:30.422 --> 00:01:31.790
-It stores enough back-up power

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:33.960
to power a home
for several days.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.028
-What?

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:36.930
-So you plug your house
into this thing.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.030
-What?

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.766
-Dude, I would
just live in the truck.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:40.834
-Yeah.

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:43.036
-It can power a house
for several days.

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:44.938
-Several or seven?

00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:48.474
Either way,
that's a lot of power.

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:50.543
-Several.
-Several days.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.878
-But then, here's the jam.

00:01:52.878 --> 00:01:54.747
So, they don't have
an engine, right?

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:56.950
Because it's a battery thing.
I don't know how it works.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.618
But all the engine is
underneath, I guess.

00:01:58.618 --> 00:01:59.686
-Right.

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:02.755
-So there is no engine
in the front.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:03.789
-Yeah.

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:07.593
-So they changed
the front to a trunk.

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:09.929
So, they're calling it --
No, I swear.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:12.332
They're calling it a frunk.
-A frunk?

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.432
-Yes!

00:02:13.432 --> 00:02:15.601
-So you'd have frunk
in your trunk?

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:16.769
-No, there is no trunk.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.137
-There's no trunk.
There's just a frunk.

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:19.873
-This frunk is -- You can put
whatever you want in --

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:21.741
You can put the trunk
in your frunk.

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:23.176
-Can you put pumpkins
in the frunk?

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:24.744
-Yes!

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.512
Oh, this holds -- Because I was
looking into it and I go,

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:29.515
"Well, talk to me
about the frunk,

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:33.786
'cause you can't fake the funk
on the nasty frunk.

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:36.523
It holds 400 pounds of payload.

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:37.590
-Payload.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.859
-Pumpkins.
-Yeah.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.060
-Payload.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.762
Power open and close. Sure.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:45.564
Power outlets in the frunk.

00:02:45.564 --> 00:02:47.066
But then check this thing out.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:49.569
So, I don't even know
if I understand this.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:50.870
Because there's no photos of it.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.806
-You're gonna make
a schematic now of the frunk?

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:55.908
-Well, I'm just trying to see
if we can --

00:02:55.908 --> 00:02:57.944
-Right.
♪♪

00:03:09.321 --> 00:03:11.958
And he kept on writing

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:14.493
for seven days and seven nights.

00:03:14.493 --> 00:03:16.295
-Alright, here you go.
-Alright.

00:03:16.295 --> 00:03:18.297
Let me see the frunk.
[ Music stops ]

00:03:18.297 --> 00:03:20.666
-Well, no, I just did that,
and that looks weird now, so...

00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:24.103
♪♪

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.038
So, I got to do that there.

00:03:26.038 --> 00:03:27.373
Alright, so,
this is kind of the idea.

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.175
Alright, look.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.376
Here is the new
Ford F-150, right?

00:03:31.376 --> 00:03:34.347
So, this is it.
-Is that "Fisco"?

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:37.516
-This is officially it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.516 --> 00:03:40.820
So, that's the -- I messed up
'cause I got too detailed.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.621
And then I go, "Oh, once I put
the steering wheel,

00:03:42.621 --> 00:03:44.557
then I got to put,
you know, the mirror in."

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:45.925
-Because I didn't --
Now that you've drawn that,

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.360
it's totally clear.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.496
I had no idea what you meant
by -- I was totally confused.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.198
I was going, "What are you
talking about?"

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.233
Wait. Where are my car keys?
I'm confused."

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:56.302
Oh, I see. It's a frunk.
-But check this out.

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.204
So, the frunk -- So, also,
check this thing out.

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:02.408
In the frunk itself,
it's water-resistant, okay?

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:04.544
So they --
And they have a drain in there.

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:05.545
-Oh.
-I went on all sort of websites.

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:07.513
-Dude, I've got it.
-Hot tub?

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:08.847
-You put your beer in there.

00:04:08.847 --> 00:04:11.817
It's a Frunky Brewster.
That's where the keep your beer.

00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:15.822
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:18.291
-Only if you're not driving.

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:19.325
Only if you're not driving.

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:20.460
-Yeah, not driving.
You're parked.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.127
-Yeah, or it's
a non-alcoholic beer.

00:04:22.127 --> 00:04:23.563
-Right. Like pumpkin beer.

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:26.632
-You can -- I did read,
you can put ice in the frunk.

00:04:26.632 --> 00:04:28.034
-Oh.
-So it's a giant cooler.

00:04:28.034 --> 00:04:29.335
-That's awesome.

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:30.370
-And as it drains -- But
you know what I'm going to do?

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.537
-What?

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:32.805
-Fill it with water
and get a little hot tub.

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:33.873
-That's what I'm saying.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:36.575
You get like two
sous vides -- right? --

00:04:36.575 --> 00:04:37.877
put them on either side.

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:39.612
-Ford -- And they -- Ford knows,

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:41.814
because I do drive
my truck everywhere.

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:44.383
I'm into this thing.
I want to go electric.

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:47.319
Find me.

00:04:47.319 --> 00:04:48.521
Yeah, find me.
Is that what I said?

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:50.023
-Yeah, "Find me. Find me, Ford."

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:51.256
-Find me.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:04:51.256 --> 00:04:54.660
So, Ford, I'll put up
the bat signal tonight,

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:55.694
and then you put up --

00:04:55.694 --> 00:04:57.029
-Frunk signal.

00:04:57.029 --> 00:04:58.764
-And you put up your frunk
signal and try to match it

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:00.699
so that our signals
are crossing.

00:05:00.699 --> 00:05:04.536
But I want to go electric.
I'm ready for this.

00:05:04.536 --> 00:05:06.672
Because you know the
F in F-150 stands for --

00:05:06.672 --> 00:05:07.673
-Frunk?

00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:09.041
-Fallon.

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:11.210
-Oh, Fallon. Yes.
-Fallon.

